WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Once upon a time, miracles really did happen.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.500
Incredible spells opened the doors of the magical land of Simsala.

3
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:20.500
A place where all the characters from fairy tales really lived.

4
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Abracadabra, Simsala Grim.

5
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
And what was that last one?

6
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Unexpected events.

7
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.500
And how do you look forward to meeting the girl of your dreams?

8
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.000
No, sir, you've never told me about that. Not a single one.

9
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Adventure, love and an unexpected event.

10
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000
I'm going to leave soon, but I'll be back quickly.

11
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Yes, you've already said that twice.

12
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.500
So what are you waiting for?

13
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Yes, but I've never been up to the surface until now and...

14
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Well, now you're allowed to go up there.

15
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Today you turn fifteen, it's time to experience life.

16
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:41.000
I'm going up to the surface now, I'll be back soon.

17
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Yes, you've said that already. Three times.

18
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.000
I'm going to the surface, I'm going to the surface.

19
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.000
You can't breathe.

20
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Thank you so much for saving our lives.

21
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.500
I'm Doctor Croki, a scientist, a philosopher.

22
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.000
And I'm Yoyo, the greatest adventurer ever.

23
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.000
You two must have strayed here from the surface of the sea.

24
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Today is your lucky day. I was just heading there.

25
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Come on, I'll show you the way.

26
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.000
I didn't think I'd see the sun again.

27
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.000
The sun is that big, yellow thing.

28
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.000
I see. And what in the name of Neptune is that?

29
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.000
A ship, that's called a ship.

30
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
And that beautiful creature standing on it?

31
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:29.000
We call that a handsome prince, if you're interested in such things.

32
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.000
I've never seen anything like it.

33
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
I think someone has fallen in love.

34
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.000
Captain Smeders, did you hear something?

35
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.500
Some beautiful voice?

36
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
It was an enchanting voice.

37
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.000
You had better go below deck, Your Highness.

38
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.000
A breeze? Well, I'm not made of sugar, you know.

39
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.000
More importantly, he's breathing and it looks like he'll survive. Wait, someone's coming.

40
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:37.000
Quickly, guys, so they don't see us.

41
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.000
Oh, are you all right?

42
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.000
What, what happened?

43
00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.000
The last thing I remember is a powerful storm and my ship.

44
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.000
You're safe now. Are you all right?

45
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.000
Nothing is broken. I feel fine.

46
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:11.000
Someone else was here. I didn't see well who it was.

47
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:17.000
This storm has stunned me. I'm Vincent. Let me introduce myself.

48
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.000
And I'm Arabella. Come on, I'll take you to the temple.

49
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Don't go, sweet prince.

50
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.000
Will I ever see him again?

51
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Of course you will.

52
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
But how, when land and sea divide us?

53
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:44.000
Oh, I wish I were a human being. I wish I had legs.

54
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:50.000
I'd walk to him and dance with him. And he'd fall in love with me.

55
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.000
That takes a powerful spell, doesn't it? To get legs, I mean.

56
00:09:55.000 --> 00:10:01.000
Yes, it takes a powerful spell. There is someone I can ask.

57
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.000
The sea witch? The sea witch?

58
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:21.000
Can you help me in any way?

59
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:26.000
You want to become a human being for love?

60
00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.500
Yes.

61
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:34.000
You know that mermaids live five times longer than humans, and you're willing to give that up?

62
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:41.000
Well, for a chance to be with my prince, yes. I want to be a human being so I can be with him.

63
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.000
So that I can be happy.

64
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.000
There is something I can give you.

65
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:55.000
A potion that will give you a human form. Yes, that's what I want.

66
00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:01.000
You'll have legs and you'll look like a human being. But it has its price.

67
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.500
I'll give you anything.

68
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.500
What's the price?

69
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.000
It will cost you your voice.

70
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:27.000
You'll be able to be with your prince, but you'll never be able to speak or sing again.

71
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Don't do it!

72
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.000
I'll do it.

73
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
You chose it yourself.

74
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.000
I hope he's the best in the world.

75
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:47.000
When you get legs, it won't be easy to use them and it will hurt.

76
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.000
But I'll have a chance to be with the prince?

77
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:59.000
Right, the rest is up to you, but if he doesn't fall in love with you, the next day you'll turn into sea foam.

78
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.000
This doesn't sound like a fair price.

79
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Will she do it or not?

80
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.000
Oh, I can't watch this anymore.

81
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.000
Who knows, maybe you won't like that prince when you get to know him.

82
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:56.000
I know you mean well, but only once in your life are you given a chance at true happiness.

83
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.000
This is my chance.

84
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.000
Are you all right?

85
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.500
You scared me.

86
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:50.000
I'm Vincent. Prince Vincent.

87
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.000
And you are...

88
00:13:53.000 --> 00:14:01.000
Can't you speak? Is that the problem?

89
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:11.000
Allow us to help. Sire, this girl thinks you're a very handsome prince.

90
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.000
Seriously?

91
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:23.000
My friend wants to say that she likes you a lot.

92
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.000
Oh, in that case, may I dance with her?

93
00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:52.000
What is that? It's my father. He has come.

94
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:59.000
We have to say goodbye, beautiful girl. I'm glad I met you. And you two as well.

95
00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.000
Maybe we'll meet again one day.

96
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:07.000
I'm sorry he had to go. I think this was a very successful meeting.

97
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Yes, I'd say he likes you.

98
00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.000
You're in a good mood, my son.

99
00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:33.000
Ah, father, I'm walking on clouds. For the first time in my life I've fallen in love.

100
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.000
I've never felt this before, at least not like this.

101
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:40.000
I'm sorry to hear that, son.

102
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.500
Yes, yes, I know.

103
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.000
I don't need to remind you.

104
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.000
No, I know.

105
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.000
You came here to marry the daughter of King Donatello.

106
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.000
To marry the king's daughter?

107
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.000
That's why you came here, that's what you agreed to, that's what you promised me.

108
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.000
I know, father, but I've fallen in love.

109
00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.000
Tomorrow you will get married.

110
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.000
No, father, I won't. I can't when I love another.

111
00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.000
I think she saved my life.

112
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.500
She saved your life?

113
00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:16.000
When my ship vanished in the storm, I think she carried me ashore.

114
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.000
Have you taken leave of your senses, son?

115
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.000
King Donatello's daughter is waiting for you outside.

116
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.000
Stop making excuses.

117
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.000
Then I'll tell her myself that I'm cancelling the wedding.

118
00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.000
You just told her that.

119
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.000
I didn't mean to show disrespect.

120
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.000
Say what you have to say to me.

121
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.000
I can't marry you, because I've fallen in love with another.

122
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.000
With another?

123
00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.000
With a beautiful girl called...

124
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
Arabella?

125
00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.000
You're King Donatello's daughter?

126
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.000
I am.

127
00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:58.000
But I thought you were a pupil in the temple.

128
00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:02.000
I am. My father sent me to the temple to study.

129
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:05.000
But I am Princess Arabella, King Donatello's daughter.

130
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.000
And I will be your queen.

131
00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.000
I've never been happier.

132
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.000
You can reverse the spell.

133
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.000
You can be a mermaid again.

134
00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.000
To get your voice back and live until the end of eternity.

135
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:51.000
But bad decisions can't just be corrected like that.

136
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.000
There is a price for it.

137
00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.000
I hope it's not bigger than the previous one.

138
00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:04.000
You have to kill the prince on the night after his wedding.

139
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.000
There is no other way.

140
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:17.000
Well, that must be a mistake. How can you ask for something like that?

141
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:21.000
Yes, the bigger the wish, the bigger the sacrifice.

142
00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:27.000
There must be some other way, with so many potions and so many spells.

143
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.000
Be grateful that there is any way at all.

144
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.000
Take this with you and think about it.

145
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.000
You don't have much time.

146
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:05.000
It's not fair. How can the little mermaid find her happiness if these are her choices?

147
00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.000
Maybe she won't be able to.

148
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.000
What choice does she have, then?

149
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:14.000
Maybe she won't be able to find happiness for herself, but she can give others their happiness.

150
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:24.000
We met in this place, and that's why it's the perfect place to be joined forever.

151
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.000
Can't we do something for her?

152
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:02.000
Maybe we can. So, where are we going?

153
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.000
To your favorite place.

154
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:11.000
Oh, all right then. This is by no means my favorite place.

155
00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.500
I was joking.

156
00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.500
You came back.

157
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.000
We came because of the little mermaid.

158
00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.500
She isn't cursed, is she?

159
00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:32.000
Yes, of course she isn't cursed. She has to make a decision.

160
00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.000
To choose one of two terrible things.

161
00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.000
That's not a decision, that's...

162
00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:43.000
There is another way for her to survive and live forever.

163
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.000
And why didn't you tell her that?

164
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Because if she knows about it, she won't succeed.

165
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.500
And what does she have to do?

166
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:58.000
She has to sacrifice herself for another, but you must not tell her.

167
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:02.000
She must not do it knowing that she'll get away with it.

168
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.000
And if she doesn't do it?

169
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.000
If she doesn't sacrifice herself for another?

170
00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.000
Then she is cursed.

171
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.000
Now go away. I've told you enough.

172
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
We have to stop her.

173
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.500
Don't do that.

174
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.500
Oh, how I wish she could talk to us.

175
00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:31.000
She wants us to follow her.

176
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Farewell, little mermaid.

177
00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.500
Now you are one of us.

178
00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.000
Daughter of the air, welcome to us.

179
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:27.000
Yoyo, did you see this?

180
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:29.500
Just as the sea witch said.

181
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.000
Simsala, Simsala, Simsala Grim!

182
00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.000
Do you think she's happy?

183
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.000
I think she's happy.

184
00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:49.000
And they lived happily ever after.
